1. Data Acquisition:
    Vital parameters of the infant such as temperature, humidity, respiration, pulse, and         crying sound are continuously monitored using respective sensors.
    The sensors are placed inside the incubator chamber for real-time data collection.

 2. Signal Processing & Control:
    The collected sensor data is sent to the microcontroller (Arduino/ESP32).
    The controller compares the values with predefined safe ranges for infants.
    If any parameter goes beyond the limit, it triggers an alert system (buzzer + display
          warning).
3. Air Purification & Environment Control:
    A fan circulates air through the HEPA filter, removing dust and harmful particles.
    This ensures a clean and safe breathing environment for the infant.
    Humidity and airflow are regulated automatically to maintain comfort.
. Data Display & Alerts
    An LCD screen displays real-time sensor values for hospital staff.
    The buzzer/alarm alerts caregivers in case of abnormalities in any parameter.

5. Power Management
    The system operates on main supply (AC power) under normal conditions.
    During power failure, an automatic relay switches to battery backup, ensuring uninterrupted    operation.
